Those of you who are especially fond of played with patched NetHacks
may appreciate this 457KB patch file encapsulating all of the following
patches of mine:

* sphere.diff - Sphere monsters make 9-square explosions; makes blessed
scroll of fire desirable.
* quaff.diff - Water elementals get a water attack; gives several
monsters an aversion to water.
* spells.diff - Monster spellcasters get more spells.
* mirrorfix.diff - Gaze attack mechanics are updated.
* poisoncloud.diff - Poison breath attacks leave poison clouds.
* construct.diff - Various polymorph forms have special values for
certain stats.
* edibility.diff - Animal forms can smell dangerous food.
* colour.diff - Monster glyph colouration is improved.
* armory.diff - New special room: dilapidated armoury.
* polysink.diff - Sink-ring effects improved.
* wallcorr.diff - Walls surround all corridors.
* whack.diff - Different verbs for hitting with certain weapons.
* juibilex.diff - The Faceless Lord's name changes.
* bigbanner.diff - ASCII splash screen.
* enchant.diff - Scrolls of enchantment.
* oilycorpse.diff - Eating certain monsters makes your hands slippery.
* baghead.diff - Put a bag on your head to blind yourself.
* labelread.diff - Special messages for reading certain objects.
* holy.diff - Holy water's effects improved; certain monsters are
"holy" or "unholy".
* breathe.diff - Wearing a towel protects you from poison gas.
* banes-sunsword.diff - Sunsword's sunlight has more effects.
* resist.diff - Half-resistance attributes added; magic resistance
split into two attributes.
* charisma.diff - Charisma stat is removed.

Here are some things that had to be considered in the production of
this patch:

* The name. Since I fully intend to release future versions with more
of my patches bundled in, the name needed to have a numeric component.
And, I didn't feel like declaring this overly large bundle of patches
to be a full-blown variant (see: PatchHack). So, I decided to call it
the "+23 Patch of Patches". May history have mercy on me.
* Which patches to include. The following patches, although among my
favourites, have not been included as I do not feel that they are
"complete" enough:
-monring.diff (I plan on implementing more stuff for monsters to put on
at some point.)
-mklev.diff (I plan on adding s'more random level generators at some
point.)
-terrain.diff (I plan on adding s'more terrain types at some point.)
-shuffled.diff (no tiles yet)
-monsteed.diff (functional but quite incomplete)
-banes-heart_of_ahriman.diff (I plan on making the Heart even more
similar to its literary counterpart.)
The remainder were excluded either because I felt that they were a bit
frivolous, or I just forgot about them.

